# Metric and imperial, over the four screens that used to disagree.
#
# The radio's own DisplayConfig.units is the only say the client has over this, and for a while
# only half the client was listening: the map drew its scale bar and its ranges in miles while
# everything behind it answered in metres whatever the setting said - a node's altitude, the
# footprint its precision describes, the smart broadcast threshold, and the MQTT section's map
# precision. The footprint was the worst of them, because the map's own selected-marker card
# draws it two lines under a range in miles.
#
# So the scene is one walk run twice. Node detail, Settings > Position, Settings > Modules >
# MQTT, then the map; first with the radio set to metric and then with it set to imperial. What
# it asks a reader to check is that the second half has no metres left in it anywhere, not that
# any one row converted correctly - that is what the ui_units suite is for.

scene demo
scale 4
delay 200
config

units metric

# Alfa Ridge is a repeater with a rounded fix, so its detail carries both of the node rows this
# is about: an altitude and a precision. It is seeds[1], and the Nodes list has three rows before
# its first node - the filter chips, the sort row and the Map (MESH_UI_NODES_LEAD_ROWS) - so its
# row is 4. Inside a detail the counts are *presses* rather than row numbers - the cursor steps
# over each group's title on its way down.
tab nodes
key down 4
key a
key down 30
hold 2200
key b
hold 300

# Settings > Position: the smart broadcast threshold, which is a length the reader picks off a
# list rather than one the mesh reported.
tab settings
key down 6
key a
key down 4
hold 2200
key b
hold 300

# Settings > Modules > MQTT: the map report's precision, which is the same ladder the node
# detail's Precision row reads and was the last place still answering in metres.
tab settings
key down 13
key a
key a
key down 9
hold 2200
key b
key b
hold 300

# The map, which was already honouring the setting - filmed so the strip holds the screen the
# other three had to agree with rather than asking a reader to remember it, and because its
# selected-marker line is where the disagreement was loudest: a range in feet and a footprint in
# metres, one space apart. The list is left with the cursor on a node, so this walks back to the
# top rather than indexing into it; the Map row is the third, under the filter chips and the
# sort row.
tab nodes
key up 6
key down 2
key a
hold 1200
key left
hold 2400
key b
hold 600

# The same four, with the radio switched over. Nothing else about the scene changes.
units imperial
hold 1400

tab nodes
key down 4
key a
key down 30
hold 2200
key b
hold 300

tab settings
key down 6
key a
key down 4
hold 2200
key b
hold 300

tab settings
key down 13
key a
key a
key down 9
hold 2200
key b
key b
hold 300

tab nodes
key up 6
key down 2
key a
hold 1200
key left
hold 2600
